INT. MINIATURE GOLF WINDMILL - DAY

The big concrete windmill at hole eighteen. Blades turning slowly. A tunnel through its base.

GRETCHEN POLLARD (50s, visor, scorecard in teeth) is wedged halfway into the tunnel on her stomach.

Her husband WALDO POLLARD (50s, bucket hat) holds her ankles.

TEENAGE ATTENDANT RUSS OYELARAN (17, name tag, vest) arrives with a rake.

LITTLE MIRABEL (8, glitter sneakers) watches from the green, club trailing.

RUSS
Ma'am, you can't go in there.

GRETCHEN (O.S.)
My ball's in there!

WALDO
She means it.

The blades turn. A blade clips Waldo's hat. He ducks. Gretchen shoots out of the tunnel, ball in hand, and the two of them tumble into Russ. All three go down in a heap. The rake clatters.

MIRABEL
Is that a hole in one?

RUSS
(from the pile)
No.

Gretchen holds up the ball like a trophy.
